  <NAME>In Vivo CRISPR Screens Identify E3 Ligase Cop1 as a Modulator of Macrophage Infiltration and Cancer Immunotherapy Target</NAME>
  <TITLE>In Vivo CRISPR Screens Identify E3 Ligase Cop1 as a Modulator of Macrophage Infiltration and Cancer Immunotherapy Target</TITLE>
  <DESCRIPTION>Cop1 regulates stability of transcription factors. We found that Cop1 can regulate the proteasomal degradation of Cebpd. We generated 4T1 breast cancer cells with CRISPR/Cas9 mediated Cop1 (gene symbol RFWD2) knockout. We used Cebpd antibody to pulldown the DNA fragments binding with Cebpd and did ChIP-seq. Overall design: Examination of Cebpd ChIP-seq under two condtions in 4T1 breast cancer cells: Rosa26 and Cop1 knockout. Additionally, we used two different gRNAs to knockout Cop1. Two replicaters per condition.</DESCRIPTION>
